.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(footprint \\\"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"59\\\") (name \\\"unconnected-(C19-Pad1)\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"C19 unconnected-_C19-Pad1_ 0 0.1u\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The part is either not mounted as a working decoupling capacitor or is physically the wrong package for the intended placement, so the decoupling intended for the EthernetAndPower section is absent or unreliable.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.4\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The netlist shows two SKW92A LAN_PORT3_TX pins shorted to the GND net, which is a clear electrical fault. A second, lower-confidence issue is that capacitor C19 has an inductor footprint and a floating pad. Many reference designators and net names differ from the specification, so the verdict rests on these direct netlist observations.\"\n}",
